 election with about $2.4 million raised and roughly $1 million in outside support. Democrat James Byrd, a state legislator, has raised about $22,000 and reported just $356 on hand, leaving him little capacity to compete.\n\nNo general-election polls are available, but every major rating outfit calls the race Solid or Safe Republican, and prediction markets give Democrats only a 2-3% chance. Wyoming's R+23 partisan lean makes a Democratic upset extraordinarily unlikely; the main question is the size of Hageman's winning margin rather than who wins.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0087, "margin": -17.16}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0045, "margin": -20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0066, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0194, "margin": -18.0}]}